{"nodes": [{"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_phase2_decisions", "label": "Phase 2 Decisions for Client Confirmation", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four Part-A decisions with resolutions, six confirmations, unanticipated decisions that changed the data, and properties that affect how results must be read."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_a1_dengue_resolution", "label": "A1: Finest-Available Dengue Spatial Resolution", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Admin-1 only would have excluded Brazil entirely, since its weekly reporting exists only at municipality level, and would have taken Colombia's modern series with it; the cost is 7,165 nodes with Brazil supplying 77% of them, mitigated by a within-country-then-across-country headline metric that does not yet exist."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_a2_dengue_case_definitions", "label": "A2: Dengue Case Definitions Accepted as Built and Disclosed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The headline multipliers up to x220 came from a raw-file group-by, not from any node's series; measured on the extracted data the genuine exposure is Mexico 2.8x and Bolivia 1.6x on 41 of 7,165 nodes, which does not justify discarding twenty years of history."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_a3_calendar_prefix_support", "label": "A3: Calendar-Prefix Ebola Support with a Fixed Cutoff", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per-district first-two-weeks support was not calendar-causal: 85% of evaluation cells lay earlier in time than the last support cell, so normalisation drew on another district's peak-epidemic magnitudes. A fixed 2014-05-24 cutoff is causal by construction."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_a4_gap_lumping", "label": "A4: Ebola Gap-Lumping Disclosed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A multi-week increment lands on the week the report arrives, so peaks are inflated and quiet weeks flattened; the alternatives either invent a distribution never observed or discard evaluation data."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_c1_running_maximum_incidence", "label": "C1: Weekly Incidence from the Running Maximum", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Differencing with a clip to zero treated a data-entry dropout as a revision and then counted the recovery as new incidence, fabricating 8,786 cases across 34 districts, 35.8% of the target, and displacing the national peak to February 2015. Differencing the running maximum conserves mass exactly and masks corrupt weeks."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_c2_first_week_masked", "label": "C2: First Observed Week of Every District Masked", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Assigning a district's cumulative total to date as its first week's new cases fabricated a backlog for every district and fed it into the normalisation of the whole held-out disease; at a first report there is no preceding figure to subtract."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_c3_split_fallback_removed", "label": "C3: Per-Node Dengue Split Fallback Removed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Re-cutting late-starting nodes on their own timeline placed their training cells inside their neighbours' test period, and a graph network aggregates over neighbours, so 475 nodes pulled test-period data into the training pass."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_c4_taiwan_aggregation", "label": "C4: Taiwan Aggregated from Townships to Counties", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No township shapefile layer exists and townships partition counties exactly, so the sum is exact; the alternative was to drop Taiwan."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_c5_influenza_adjacency_diagonal", "label": "C5: Influenza Adjacency Diagonal Zeroed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "As shipped, influenza nodes carried twice the self-weight of dengue nodes inside the shared model, a structural signature from which the model could infer the disease."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_c6_ebola_cross_border_edges", "label": "C6: Ebola Graph Keeps Cross-Border Connections", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The 2014 epidemic was a single outbreak across three contiguous countries and the Gueckedou-Lofa-Kailahun tri-border area is its defining transmission pathway, so a country-separated graph would sever exactly the connections that carry the signal."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_c7_sierra_leone_labels", "label": "C7: Three Sierra Leonean Labels That Are Not Districts", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Port was Port Loko truncated and was merged; Western Area is the parent of two districts already present and would have counted the same cases three times; Freetown has one report and no boundary. Client asked for a single Western Area node instead of dropping it."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_c8_dengue_per_country_splits", "label": "C8: Dengue Splits Cut Per Country", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A single global chronological cut would have given zero training data to five countries silently, with no error raised."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_c9_geographic_covariates_withheld", "label": "C9: Geographic Covariates Withheld from the Shared Model", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The three diseases occupy disjoint parts of the world, so a coordinate identifies the disease outright; populating centroids for all three did not make them safe to expose."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_b6_mobility_not_used", "label": "B6: Mobility Data Not Used for Any Disease", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A real commuting matrix exists for Japan but not for dengue or Ebola, so attaching it to influenza alone would let the model identify which disease it is looking at."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_d1_zero_variance_guard", "label": "D1: Zero-Variance Normalisation Guard Fixed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A blanket scale of one fired on 400 dengue nodes and left the 76 that vary in the held-out period un-normalised; a constant-in-training node now takes its country's pooled training statistics."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_d2_japan_zero_dengue", "label": "D2: Twenty-Nine Japanese Prefectures Report Zero Dengue", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The zeros are true and the nodes remain valid graph neighbours, but under a country-averaged headline Japan carries one twelfth of the score while 62% of its nodes are trivially predictable."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_d6_dengue_block_diagonal_graph", "label": "D6: The Dengue Graph Forbids Cross-Border Edges", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Justified on the false ground that the dengue countries are not adjacent; defensible as a deliberate simplification that keeps mixed spatial resolutions safe to combine, but it severs real transmission corridors and costs real signal."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_negative_control_gates", "label": "Negative Controls on Every Gate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The suite grew to 86 gates and six negative controls, each carrying a deliberately planted failure it must detect, because the number of tests passing was on its own worthless as evidence."}], "edges": [{"source": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_phase2_decisions", "target": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_a1_dengue_resolution", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_phase2_decisions", "target": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_a2_dengue_case_definitions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_phase2_decisions", "target": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_a3_calendar_prefix_support", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_phase2_decisions", "target": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_a4_gap_lumping", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_phase2_decisions", "target": "progress_decisions_client_decisions_c1_running_maximum_incidence", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/client_decisions.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decis